    
       COMMAND TO FETCH FILES FROM MY GIT REPO
  
  1. cd "path\to\folder" (local folder I'm pulling the files to)
  
  2. git init (Initialize git)
  
  3. git remote add origin "https://github.com/username/your_repo" (Add the repo as remote named origin)
  
  4. git fetch origin
     git checkout -b "local_branch" "origin/remote_branch"
       (This will create a local branch tracking the remote branch)
       
  5. git pull origin zsh (Pull all files from the remote branch into the local folder)